[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
so every report about a wrong date landed in it. Read by tenant, form and body, the reports
show two problems. Each now has a ticket of its own.

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/adxable/what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/adxable/what-it-shows/issues/2',
  }}
/>

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 closes only the parser row. The booking-v3 hint needs its own fix,
and its reporters are still waiting on a ticket marked known.
</Callout>

## How the reports split

- **parser**: the tenant writes the day first and the shared parser reads the month first. The
  date comes back with day and month swapped.
- **hint**: the report came through a booking-v3 form, whose hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`. People typed
  month first because the form told them to.

Intake's tag guesses from the reporter's browser, so the table ignores it and places each report by its
tenant, as `causes.ts` does. The export repeats some rows; each report counts once, by id.

